# Copy to `.env` (or `.env.production`) before `npm run build`.
# Vite only exposes variables prefixed with VITE_ to the client bundle.
#
# Every one of these can also be supplied at run time as a URL query parameter,
# which overrides the built-in value and is remembered in localStorage — handy
# for pointing a already-deployed build at a different relay while testing. The
# two TURN credentials are the exception: they are read from the URL of the
# session using them and are never written to localStorage. See
# src/net/NetConfig.js.
#
# Nothing here configures the signalling relay itself. `tools/signal-server.mjs`
# reads SIGNAL_* from its own process environment, not from this file, and a
# public deployment must set at least SIGNAL_ALLOWED_ORIGINS — see
# "Reference: operating the relay" in docs/MULTIPLAYER.md.

# --- signalling -------------------------------------------------------------
# The WebSocket relay that hands a room code's offer/answer across.
# Runtime override: ?signal=wss://...
# MUST be wss:// if the game itself is served over https.
VITE_SIGNAL_URL=wss://your-relay.example.com

# --- TURN -------------------------------------------------------------------
# Without this, players behind symmetric NAT (lots of corporate, university and
# mobile networks) will silently fail to connect. Comma-separated; offering
# UDP, TCP and TLS-on-443 is what gets through restrictive firewalls.
# Runtime override: ?turn=...&turnuser=...&turnpass=...
#
# The username and credential set here are BAKED INTO THE BUNDLE: anyone who
# loads the game can read them out of the JavaScript. Ship one only when you
# accept that every player has it.
#
# For probe runs, prefer ?turnuser=/?turnpass= on the page URL — the page holds
# those for the session and never writes them to localStorage. But check what
# your probe records first: tools/coopprobe.mjs on this branch has no credential
# flags and no redactor, and it writes the two page URLs verbatim into its JSON
# record (`urls.host` / `urls.client`), so anything you put in a query string
# lands in that file. The redacting probe arrives with the parked
# slice/mp-p4-remote-network slice; until it merges, use throwaway credentials
# for any probe run whose record is committed.
VITE_TURN_URLS=turn:your-turn.example.com:3478,turn:your-turn.example.com:3478?transport=tcp,turns:your-turn.example.com:443
VITE_TURN_USERNAME=
VITE_TURN_CREDENTIAL=

# --- testing ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Set to `relay` to forbid direct connections entirely, forcing all traffic
# through TURN. The only reliable way to prove a TURN config actually works.
# Runtime override: ?ice=relay
VITE_ICE_POLICY=
